{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>לא</b> — Rabbi Moses the Kohen says: it is like <b>משאת מאומה לא ישלוט בו נושה</b> (a debt of anything, a creditor shall not have power over him), meaning <b>לא ישיא</b> (he shall not impose). Some say: it is from the root of <b>זדון לבך השיאך</b> (the presumption of your heart has lifted you)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's first example, משאת מאומה לא ישלוט בו נושה, does not correspond to any biblical verse; it may be his own paraphrase or a rabbinic dictum, rendered here literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:34.347112026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}